1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,160
Does this pull request create new access to a privileged role?

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:12,760
Review sees one changed word on line 27: false becomes true.

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:17,360
The risk is what it completes: older grants that each look harmless.

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,460
The repository's AttackGraph AI check fails, and says why.

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:26,860
This line lets the CI deploy user run code as the deployment admin role.

6
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,960
The check makes no AWS calls and needs no secrets.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,160
AttackGraph AI compares the current and the proposed configuration.

8
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,360
This change widens iam:PassRole and completes all 7 conditions of a route to admin.

9
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:50,860
The demo runs the same check on the same one-line change.

10
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:54,793
Apply the suggested fix: the fix commit reverts the line.

11
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:58,993
The check runs again on the fix commit, and passes.

12
00:00:59,033 --> 00:01:04,293
Inside the check: high-risk paths go from 0 to 1, and coverage is complete.

13
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:09,693
The route: CI deploy user, through the post-build hook, to the deployment admin role.

14
00:01:09,733 --> 00:01:13,727
The amber arrow is the one changed fact: false becomes true.

15
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:18,527
A route counts only when every condition holds: here, 7 of 7.

16
00:01:18,567 --> 00:01:22,527
Six already held, one of them a stated scenario assumption.

17
00:01:22,567 --> 00:01:25,827
The new permission was the missing piece.

18
00:01:25,867 --> 00:01:31,860
One live call to Amazon Nova Pro on Amazon Bedrock.

19
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:37,893
The live reply, with its request ID. The page maps placeholders back to names.

20
00:01:37,933 --> 00:01:41,893
The model sees placeholder IDs, never names.

21
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:45,593
A reply that cites anything outside the evidence is discarded.

22
00:01:45,633 --> 00:01:49,793
The engine decides findings, severity and fixes. The model only explains.

23
00:01:52,467 --> 00:01:57,460
The engine tests the fix: revoke that one permission on a copy, rerun everything.

24
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:02,560
High-risk paths drop from 1 to 0. Normal access still passes: 2 of 2.

25
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:07,060
Verified in this model, not promised for a real account.

26
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:12,793
The limits are up front: synthetic data only, nothing deployed or executed.

27
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:17,127
Two explicit rules, not all of AWS.

28
00:02:17,167 --> 00:02:20,527
An unknown is never reported as safe.
